    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="0927" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg845"/>

                <head>Mr. Motley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 177.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 21, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to state that I have just
                    received a note from Count Mensdorff, in answer to my note of date May 6, a copy
                    of which was forwarded with my despatch No. 170, of date May 8.</p>
                <p>I have prepared a careful translation of the minister’s note, which, together
                    with a copy of the original, I transmit with this despatch.</p>
                <p>I cannot doubt that both the contents and friendly spirit of this communication
                    from the imperial royal government will give sincere satisfaction to the United
                    States government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. LOTHROP MOTLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d757-a1.xml" xpointer="d757-a1"/>
            </div>
